      "name": "Keto Pecan Pie Cookies Recipe",
      "description": "Transform the rich, decadent essence of a classic Southern pecan pie into a perfectly portioned, keto-friendly cookie that satisfies both your sweet tooth and dietary goals. Each cookie is a carefully crafted miniature dessert that captures the essence of traditional pecan pie while adhering to low-carb nutritional guidelines. The delicate almond flour base provides a tender, buttery foundation that serves as the perfect canvas for the rich, caramelized pecan filling, creating a dessert that’s both nostalgic and innovative.\n\nWhat sets these cookies apart is their delightful design: each cookie features a carefully crafted well or indent that cradles a luscious pecan pie filling, creating a miniature dessert experience in every bite. The almond flour base offers a subtle nuttiness that harmonizes beautifully with the toasted pecans, while the allulose ensures a sweet profile without the carbohydrate load of traditional sugar. Each cookie becomes a personal-sized indulgence, allowing you to enjoy the complex flavors of pecan pie. Whether you’re following a strict ketogenic diet, looking to reduce your sugar intake, or simply seeking a sophisticated twist on a classic dessert, these Keto Pecan Pie Cookies promise to be a game-changing addition to your baking repertoire.\n\nRead the full recipe with full nutrition breakdown and step-by-step pictures over at:\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nIngredients:\nCookie Base:\n2 cups almond flour, sifted\n1/4 cup butter\n1 large egg\n1/4 cup cream cheese, room temperature\n1/3 cup allulose\n1 teaspoon vanilla extract\n1/2 teaspoon baking powder\n1/4 teaspoon xanthan gum\n\nPecan Pie Filling:\n5 tablespoon butter\n1/2 cup allulose\n1 1/4 cup pecans, chopped\n1/3 cup heavy cream\n1/2 teaspoon cinnamon\n1 teaspoon vanilla extract\nsalt, to taste, ~1/8 teaspoon\n\nNutrition Summary: This makes a total of 12 servings of Keto Pecan Pie Cookies. Each serving comes out to be 314 calories, 30.2g fats, 2.7g net carbs, and 6.1g protein.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSee more keto recipes, knowledge and tips on the website to keep your weight loss going strong.\n\nEverything you need to know about the keto diet:\n\nGetting started? Everything you need is here:\n\nWe also make things easy with this 14 day diet plan:\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nFollow Ruled.Me for more tasty food:",
